      "mathematical_review": "For t_n=2^-1/n, P(K_n=0)=t_n^n=1/2. The root-n error equals -sqrt(n) on that event and zero otherwise, so every fixed-bound tail eventually has probability1/2; it is not tight. A fixed centered L2 IID influence expansion would force weak convergence and tightness, so such an expansion cannot hold. This moving-terminal-time example supplies no functional limit or fixed-horizon uniform expansion.",
